## Original Content
The world largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis. But the exodus has not stopped, aid is shrinking and a generation of refugees is growing up with little prospect of going home.<br />

## Summary
The Rohingya crisis has entered a dangerous phase nine years after it began, with global attention fading away. Despite this, the refugee exodus continues, aid is declining, and a new generation is growing up with no realistic prospect of returning home.

## Key Points
- Global attention has largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis.
- The exodus of Rohingya refugees has not stopped.
- Aid for the refugees is shrinking.
- A generation of refugees is growing up with little hope of returning home.


